                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.wisc.edu/~andreic/publications/AinfinityLG.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %h4#defects Defects
          %p General defects of B-twisted affine LG models were first discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ilka+Brunner"}> Ilka Brunner
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Roggenkamp"} Daniel Roggenkamp
              = succeed "," do
                %em B-type defects in Landau–Ginzburg models
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0707.0922"} arXiv:0707.0922
          %p The graded pivotal bicategory of B-twisted affine LG models is studied in detail in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nils+Carqueville"}> Nils Carqueville
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Murfet"} Daniel Murfet
              = succeed "," do
                %em Adjunctions and defects in Landau-Ginzburg models
              %strong 289
              (2016) 480-566 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2015.03.033"}> doi:10.1016/j.aim.2015.03.033
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1208.1481"} arXiv:1208.1481
          %p
            and described in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+logic"} linear logic
            and the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+interactions"} geometry of interactions
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Murfet"}> Daniel Murfet
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The cut operation on matrix factorisations
              %p
                %strong 222
                7 (2018) 1911-1955 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1402.4541"}> arXiv:1402.4541
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpaa.2017.08.014"} doi:10.1016/j.jpaa.2017.08.014
          %p A proposed Landau-Ginzburg model for strict 2-groups:
          %ul
            %li
              Ruizhi Liu, Ran Luo, Yi-Nan Wang.
              %em Higher-Matter and Landau-Ginzburg Theory of Higher-Group Symmetries
              (2024). (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.03974"}> arXiv:2406.03974
